<title>USA: Teamsters, UPS talks to restart at 2 p.m. EDT.</title>
<headline>Teamsters, UPS talks to restart at 2 p.m. EDT.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Negotiations between United Parcel Service and the Teamsters are to reopen at 2 p.m. EDT (1800 GMT), a Teamsters spokeswoman said Thursday.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said the talks would be held at the Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service.</p>
<p>&quot;They start at two,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>About 185,000 Teamsters have been on strike against UPS since Monday.</p>
</text>
